.TH ZEX-INSPECT 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-inspect \- deep-inspect an installed package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zex inspect
.I <package>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex inspect
displays detailed information about an installed package:
.TP
\(bu
Package identity: name, version, description, license, maintainer.
.TP
\(bu
Installation metadata: tier origin, libc target, build type, install date.
.TP
\(bu
Disk usage: file count, total size.
.TP
\(bu
Installed file locations (from receipt).
.TP
\(bu
Shared library dependencies detected via
.BR readelf (1).
.TP
\(bu
Integrity check: verifies every declared file is present on disk.
.PP
Packages that are part of the immutable syshub base are inspected from the
.I /overlayer/syshub/engine/services/syshub.toml
manifest.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Package found and inspected.
.TP
.B 1
Package not installed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
    zex inspect ripgrep
    zex inspect bash
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-doctor (1),
.BR readelf (1)
